Notebook[{
Cell["CartogramWL update \[LongDash] Alaska, Hawaii, and a faster default", \
"Title",ExpressionUUID->"16ba5185-4ca0-4df7-a0ed-f19ff4b08e59"],

Cell["\<\
A short follow-up note on the diffusion-cartogram package introduced in the \
main post: what the recent commits changed, and where to download the current \
version.\
\>", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"0dbe7b3a-2f07-4386-961c-5697c7cd1372"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Marco Thiel, April 2026 \[LongDash] ",
 ButtonBox["github.com/mthiel74/Contiguous-Cartograms",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://github.com/mthiel74/Contiguous-Cartograms"], None}]
}], "Text",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontSlant->Italic,ExpressionUUID->"e05daa4b-aa99-4044-aed4-65a28ef08aea"],

Cell["1. What changed", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"71e14a7e-59a3-4cbd-95ea-eb770d265c8f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Since the original post the package ",
 StyleBox["CartogramWL", "Input"],
 " has picked up several improvements that are relevant if you tried the \
earlier version. The biggest single visible change is that ",
 StyleBox["WorldCartogram", "Input"],
 " now correctly handles multi-part countries \[LongDash] in particular, the \
United States is represented as the contiguous 48 states plus Alaska and \
Hawaii rather than just the lower 48."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"77f07dd6-6dc9-4204-8d79-c31aa810c009"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["\[Bullet] ",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "Alaska, Hawaii and other \"multi-part\" countries are now rendered and \
deformed correctly. ",
 StyleBox["CountryData[\"UnitedStates\", \"Polygon\"]", "Input"],
 " only returns the contiguous 48 states; a new helper ",
 StyleBox["CountryPolygonRings[c]", "Input"],
 " splices the Alaska and Hawaii ",
 StyleBox["AdministrativeDivision", "Input"],
 " polygons back in before rasterisation. The same hook can be used to bring \
in France's overseas departments, Portugal's Azores/Madeira, Denmark's \
Greenland, and so on.\n",
 StyleBox["\[Bullet] ",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "A new ",
 StyleBox["PerformanceGoal -> \"Speed\"", "Input"],
 " default pre-computes a handful of log-spaced density/gradient snapshots \
and linearly interpolates between them while the advection integrator runs. \
That cuts a full world cartogram from about 5 minutes to under a minute with \
sub-pixel agreement. ",
 StyleBox["PerformanceGoal -> \"Quality\"", "Input"],
 " restores the bit-exact baseline.\n",
 StyleBox["\[Bullet] ",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "Any ",
 StyleBox["ColorData[...]", "Input"],
 " gradient can be supplied as ",
 StyleBox["\"ColorFunction\"", "Input"],
 "; ",
 StyleBox["\"Background\" -> \"Satellite\"", "Input"],
 " textures each country with the corresponding patch of Wolfram's satellite \
imagery and deforms the imagery along with the cartogram.\n",
 StyleBox["\[Bullet] ",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "The metric argument is flexible: a recognised string, any CountryData \
property name, a custom ",
 StyleBox["Function[c, ...]", "Input"],
 ", or an ",
 StyleBox["Association", "Input"],
 " like ",
 StyleBox["<|\"Germany\" -> 83., \"France\" -> 67.5, ...|>", "Input"],
 " with missing countries optionally drawn in grey via ",
 StyleBox["\"MissingCountries\" -> \"ShowGrey\"", "Input"],
 ".\n",
 StyleBox["\[Bullet] ",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "A ",
 StyleBox["CartogramDistortionGrid[cart]", "Input"],
 " helper returns the warped-grid lines so you can visualise the deformation \
field directly."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"013cd82d-97f2-4d7c-8d1f-de93499c3abd"],

Cell["2. Alaska and Hawaii: what this actually looks like", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"da1a7d25-0a48-47d4-a190-4998f4ab5b7a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The figure below shows the GDP cartogram of North America rendered twice \
with identical parameters. In the left column the US polygon comes straight \
from ",
 StyleBox["CountryData", "Input"],
 "; in the right column it comes from the new ",
 StyleBox["CountryPolygonRings", "Input"],
 ". Top row is the geographic input (US highlighted in orange), bottom row is \
the cartogram. With the fix the United States ends up with 28 mainland rings \
+ 77 Alaska rings (mainland + Aleutians) + 8 Hawaiian rings, all sharing a \
single country value, and Alaska and Hawaii inflate alongside the mainland \
instead of being silently dropped."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1625f7e9-a28a-4e24-8907-82cc65c6554a"],

